IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `wia-types`
IMPORT `wia-days`

-- Water Industry Act 1991 (UK) — GOAL 1: CONNECTIONS (ss 45-51, 106).
-- Source: ../registers/source-bundle/ukpga-1991-56.txt.
-- The customer asks: "Must the water company connect my premises to its
-- main, by when, and what conditions can it impose; what interest is due on
-- my deposit; can the sewerage company still refuse my drain?"

§ `Goal 1 — connections`

-- s 47(3): "A condition shall not be imposed ... except by a counter-notice
-- served ... before the end of the period of fourteen days beginning with the
-- day after the service of the connection notice." By the service day + 14.
@ref s 47(3)
@export Was a condition of connection imposed in time under s 47(3) of the Water Industry Act 1991 (UK)? Only by a counter-notice served within the fourteen days beginning with the day after the connection notice was served. DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN c IS A `Connection notice`  @desc The connection notice and any counter-notice imposing conditions
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `conditions were imposed in time for` c IF
    CONSIDER c's `conditions counter-notice served on`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST k  THEN k AT MOST `the day` 14 `days after` (c's `notice served on`)

-- s 45(1)-(2): the duty arises on a connection notice by the owner or
-- occupier of premises with (or for) a building, for a domestic supply, to a
-- main that is neither a trunk main nor for non-domestic supply only, once
-- the conditions validly imposed under ss 47-50 are satisfied.
@ref s 45(1)-(2), 47(3)
@export Has the water undertaker's duty to connect my premises to its main arisen under s 45 of the Water Industry Act 1991 (UK)? Yes on a connection notice by the owner or occupier of premises consisting of (or to have) a building, for a domestic supply, to a main that is neither a trunk main nor solely for non-domestic supply, once any conditions imposed in time under s 47 are satisfied. DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN c IS A `Connection notice`  @desc The connection notice, the premises, the main and any conditions
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the duty to connect has arisen for` c IF
        c's `served by the owner or occupier`
    AND c's `premises with or for a building`
    AND c's `for a domestic supply`
    AND NOT (c's `the main is a trunk main or for non-domestic supply only`)
    AND (    NOT (`conditions were imposed in time for` c)
         OR  NOT (c's `conditions satisfied on` EQUALS NOTHING))

GIVEN a IS A DATE, m IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the later of` a `and maybe` m MEANS
    CONSIDER m
    WHEN NOTHING THEN a
    WHEN JUST x  THEN `the later of` a x

-- s 51(6): "the day after whichever is the latest of" the notice, any
-- pipe-laid notice, and the day all conditions are satisfied.
@ref s 51(6)
GIVEN c IS A `Connection notice`
GIVETH A DATE
`the relevant day for` c MEANS
    `the day` 1 `days after` latest
    WHERE
        withPipe MEANS `the later of` (c's `notice served on`) `and maybe` (c's `pipe-laid notice served on`)
        latest MEANS
            IF `conditions were imposed in time for` c
            THEN `the later of` withPipe `and maybe` (c's `conditions satisfied on`)
            ELSE withPipe

-- s 51(1)(b): a pipe already laid — "before the end of the period of
-- fourteen days beginning with the relevant day", so by the relevant day +
-- 13. s 51(1)(a), (2): otherwise "as soon as reasonably practicable", presumed
-- to be "the period of twenty-one days beginning with the relevant day", so
-- by the relevant day + 20 (F2).
@ref s 51(1)-(2), (6)
@export The last day by which the water undertaker must make my connection under s 51 of the Water Industry Act 1991 (UK): 14 days beginning with the relevant day where the whole service pipe was already laid, otherwise (as presumed) 21 days beginning with it; the relevant day is the day after the latest of the notice, any notice that my part of the pipe is laid, and the satisfying of the conditions. NOTHING if the duty has not arisen. DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN c IS A `Connection notice`  @desc The connection notice, the pipe, and any conditions
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the last day to connect for` c MEANS
    IF `the duty to connect has arisen for` c
    THEN IF c's `the service pipe was already laid`
         THEN JUST (`the day` 13 `days after` (`the relevant day for` c))
         ELSE JUST (`the day` 20 `days after` (`the relevant day for` c))
    ELSE NOTHING

-- s 48(1): interest "on every sum of 50p so deposited for every three months
-- during which it remains in the hands of the undertaker" — whole 50p sums
-- and whole periods of three months (F3).
@ref s 48(1)
@export The interest the water undertaker must pay on my deposit under s 48 of the Water Industry Act 1991 (UK): the rate determined, for every whole 50p deposited, for every whole three months the money stays with it. DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN s IS A `Security deposit`  @desc The amount deposited, the rate per 50p per three months, and the days deposited and returned
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the interest on my deposit` s MEANS
    fifties TIMES quarters TIMES s's `interest per 50p per three months`
    WHERE
        fifties MEANS FLOOR (2 TIMES s's `amount deposited`)
        quarters MEANS `whole three-month periods from` (s's `deposited on`) `to` (s's `returned on`) `counted` 0

GIVEN a IS A DATE, b IS A DATE, k IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`whole three-month periods from` a `to` b `counted` k MEANS
    IF `add months` a (3 TIMES (k PLUS 1)) AT MOST b
    THEN `whole three-month periods from` a `to` b `counted` (k PLUS 1)
    ELSE k

-- s 106(4): "At any time within twenty-one days after a sewerage undertaker
-- receives a notice ... the undertaker may by notice ... refuse".
@ref s 106(4)
@export The last day the sewerage undertaker may refuse to let my drain communicate with its public sewer, under s 106(4) of the Water Industry Act 1991 (UK): 21 days after it received my notice. DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN s IS A `Sewer notice`  @desc The day the undertaker received my notice
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to refuse my sewer connection for` s MEANS
    `the day` 21 `days after` (s's `received by the sewerage undertaker on`)

@ref s 106(4)
@export Was the sewerage undertaker's refusal given in time under s 106(4) of the Water Industry Act 1991 (UK)? DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN s IS A `Sewer notice`  @desc The day it received my notice and the day of any refusal
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the refusal was in time for` s IF
    CONSIDER s's `refusal notice given on`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST r  THEN r AT MOST `the last day to refuse my sewer connection for` s
